  "prompt_text": "The figure illustrates a concept for space-based computing built around two complementary satellite systems: an orbital edge data centre and an orbital cloud data centre. The edge system is shown as a small group of sensing satellites that collect data in space and process it near the source using specialized AI accelerators. The cloud system is depicted as a larger constellation of computing satellites with more general-purpose server capacity, intended to handle broader processing tasks for both space-generated and ground-offloaded workloads.\n\nBoth orbital systems are powered by solar energy and cooled by radiative heat loss to space, emphasizing a carbon-neutral design. Arrows between the two clusters and a central “data communication” loop indicate exchange of data and coordination in orbit. Additional links connect the orbital infrastructure with ground stations, terrestrial cloud data centres, and end users on Earth, suggesting a hybrid architecture in which some computation happens in space and some remains on the ground.\n\nOverall, the image compares edge-style, application-specific orbital processing with cloud-style, general-purpose orbital processing, and presents them as an integrated extension of terrestrial digital infrastructure.",
